---
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import AssistantSetup from "../components/AssistantSetup.astro";
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Milton makes every AI write like you"
  description="Your writing style, kept as approved samples and a few rules, in one place every AI assistant can read. Useful with one assistant or several. Free early access; planned launch price $5.01/month."
>
  <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="headline">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">// Did you get that memo?</p>
      <h1 id="headline">Every AI should write like you.</h1>
      <p class="intro">
        Your emails, messages, and posts, in your voice, whichever assistant
        drafts them. Milton keeps the writing you approved and the rules around
        it. Connect Milton. Ask “did you get that memo?”
      </p>
      <p class="hero-aside">
        Everyone else is building superintelligence. We’re asking it to stop
        using em dashes.
      </p>
      <div class="actions action-row">
        <a class="button" href="https://app.meetmilton.com/login">
          Try Milton free <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
        </a>
        <AssistantSetup />
      </div>
      <p class="access-note small-note">
        Free during early access. No credit card.{" "}
        <a href="#pricing">$5.01/month at launch.</a>
      </p>
    </div>
    <figure class="memo-example">
      <div class="memo-exchange">
        <dl>
          <div>
            <dt>You</dt>
            <dd>“For the 100th f-ing time: no em dashes.”</dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>Assistant</dt>
            <dd>“Absolutely—I’ll remember that.”</dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>Milton</dt>
            <dd>We’ll put it in writing.</dd>
          </div>
        </dl>
      </div>
      <div class="sheet">
        <div class="sheet-bar">
          <span>Your writing</span>
          <span>Example</span>
        </div>
        <div class="example-name">
          Cover sheet <span>Email report</span>
        </div>
        <div class="sheet-content">
          <h2 class="sheet-heading">Here’s how I write.</h2>
          <ul class="instruction-list">
            <li>No em dashes. Final warning.</li>
            <li>Oxford comma. Always.</li>
            <li>Emails: three short paragraphs, then “Best,” and my name.</li>
            <li>Approved sample: the follow-up I actually sent.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </figure>
  </section>
  <div class="assistant-strip">
    <span>One assistant or several.</span>
    <div class="assistant-guides">
      <nav aria-label="Assistant setup guides">
        <span>
          <a href="/setup#claude">Claude</a> ·{" "}
          <a href="/setup#chatgpt">ChatGPT</a>
        </span>
        <span>
          <a href="/setup#claude-code">Claude Code</a> ·{" "}
          <a href="/setup#codex">Codex</a> · <a href="/setup#cursor">Cursor</a>
        </span>
      </nav>
      <div>
        <p class="guide-status" id="unverified-guides">
          Guides only; not yet verified with Milton:
        </p>
        <nav
          aria-label="Unverified assistant setup guides"
          aria-describedby="unverified-guides"
        >
          <span>
            <a href="/setup#claude-duet">Claude Duet</a> ·{" "}
            <a href="/setup#grok-bot">Grok Bot</a> ·{" "}
            <a href="/setup#muse">Muse</a>
          </span>
        </nav>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="scope-heading">
    <p class="eyebrow">// Less rewriting</p>
    <h2 id="scope-heading">
      Your assistants should write like you before they write for you.
    </h2>
    <p class="section-lead">
      When an assistant drafts an email, a message, or a post in your name, it
      should sound like you. Milton keeps the writing you approved and the rules
      around it on file, so every draft starts closer to your voice.
    </p>
    <div class="use-cases">
      <article class="use-case">
        <h3>The voice you carry.</h3>
        <p>
          Samples you approved: the follow-up you actually sent, the connection
          note that worked. Rules for what a sample cannot show: greetings,
          sign-offs, length, and the phrases you never use.
        </p>
        <p class="sample-rule">
          “Use at most one exclamation point, in the opening line.”
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="use-case">
        <h3>The context you keep separate.</h3>
        <p>
          Project files, conversation history, and factual memory stay with the
          tools you use for that work. Milton holds how you write, not what you
          know.
        </p>
        <p class="sample-rule">
          Your writing and coding assistants can share your email voice without
          sharing their project histories.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section" id="how-it-works" aria-labelledby="how-heading">
    <p class="eyebrow">// Less repeating. Less paperwork.</p>
    <h2 id="how-heading">Tell it once. Keep it on file.</h2>
    <ol class="steps">
      <li>
        <h3>Connect your assistant.</h3>
        <p>
          Add Milton through your assistant’s MCP or connector settings and sign
          in to your Milton account.
        </p>
        <p>
          <a href="/setup">Find your setup instructions →</a>
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Approve a draft. Keep it.</h3>
        <p>
          When a draft is right, say so. Your assistant offers to save it as a
          sample. Correct the same thing twice and it proposes a rule. Starting
          from scratch? A short setup asks which greeting, sign-off, and length
          are yours.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Bring it to the next chat.</h3>
        <p>
          Ask “did you get that memo?” to load your cover sheet and the report
          that fits: email, chat, post, document, or speech. Tell your assistant
          what to add, correct, or remove as your writing changes.
        </p>
      </li>
    </ol>
    <figure class="conversation sheet">
      <div class="sheet-bar">
        <span>One sample, two conversations</span>
        <span>Illustrative example</span>
      </div>
      <div class="conversation-steps sheet-content">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">You, today</p>
          <blockquote>
            “Send it.” Your assistant: “Save this as a sample?” You: “Yes.”
          </blockquote>
          <p class="conversation-note small-note">
            Milton files the email, exactly as approved, under your email
            report.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">You, next time</p>
          <blockquote>
            “Did you get that memo? Draft a reply to this thread.”
          </blockquote>
          <p class="conversation-note small-note">
            Your assistant reads the email report: your sample first, then your
            rules.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </figure>
    <p class="reading-note small-note">
      <strong class="memo-limit">
        We distribute the memo. We cannot make everyone read it.
      </strong>
      Ask your assistant to read your Milton cover sheet when you start work. It
      isn’t automatically included in every chat, and following it is still up
      to the assistant.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section
    class="section control-section"
    id="your-preferences"
    aria-labelledby="control-heading"
  >
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">// You stay in control</p>
      <h2 id="control-heading">We won’t take your stapler.</h2>
      <p class="portability-copy">
        Read your cover sheet and reports. Download them as TPS.md. Run Milton
        yourself.
      </p>
      <p class="portability-aside">
        We’d prefer you keep paying us, but apparently that’s not a retention
        strategy.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a href="https://github.com/zoneofdanger/milton">Read the source ↗</a>
      </p>
    </div>
    <figure class="employee-testimonial" id="employee-testimonial">
      <p class="eyebrow">// Fictional employee testimonial</p>
      <blockquote>
        “Milton lets me say ‘Did you get that memo?’ to software. I have never
        felt more qualified for management.”
      </blockquote>
      <figcaption>
        <strong>Michael Bolton</strong>
        <span>Senior Founding AI Forward Deployed Product Engineer</span>
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </section>
  <section
    class="section pricing"
    id="pricing"
    aria-labelledby="pricing-heading"
  >
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">// One plan. We resisted making three columns.</p>
      <h2 id="pricing-heading">Less repeating yourself.</h2>
      <p class="section-lead">
        One plan for your writing voice, whether you use one assistant or
        several.
      </p>
      <p class="reading-note small-note">
        Early access is free while we prepare paid subscriptions. No card is
        required, and signing up today won’t charge you.
      </p>
      <p class="reading-note small-note">
        After your free trial, subscribe to keep assistant access. You can still
        view and download your report without a subscription.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="sheet price-card">
      <div class="sheet-bar">
        <span>Planned launch pricing</span>
      </div>
      <div class="sheet-content">
        <p class="price">
          <strong>$5.01</strong> <span>USD / month</span>
        </p>
        <p>Five dollars for Milton. One cent for accounting.</p>
        <p>30 days free. No credit card required.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Enterprise-grade asking nicely.</li>
          <li>Synergy, pending approval.</li>
          <li>A founder who has mistaken this for a company.</li>
        </ul>
        <a class="button" href="https://app.meetmilton.com/login">
          Try free early access <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section faq" aria-labelledby="faq-heading">
    <p class="eyebrow">// A few things to know</p>
    <h2 id="faq-heading">Before you connect.</h2>
    <details>
      <summary>Is it useful if I only use Claude?</summary>
      <p>
        Yes. Keep one voice across conversations with the same assistant, with
        samples it can imitate instead of adjectives it has to interpret.
        Connecting another assistant later is optional.
      </p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>How is this different from memory or Supermemory?</summary>
      <p>
        Memory tools store facts and preferences. Milton stores how you write:
        writing you approved, quoted exactly, and the rules you asked for, in a
        form every assistant can read. Keep facts, documents, and project
        history in the tools you already use.
      </p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Why not use custom instructions or AGENTS.md?</summary>
      <p>
        Those can work well. Milton gives you one place to keep your voice
        without copying changes between assistants or project files. Keep
        project-specific setup in those files, and ask your assistant to read
        Milton for how you write.
      </p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Which assistants can I connect?</summary>
      <p>
        Milton uses MCP. Your assistant needs support for a remote MCP server,
        sign-in, and both reading and saving through tools. Availability depends
        on your assistant, plan, and workspace settings.{" "}
        <a href="/setup">Check the setup guide before signing up.</a>
      </p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>What’s the cover sheet? What’s a report?</summary>
      <p>
        The cover sheet holds the rules true of all your writing and an index of
        five reports: email, chat, post, document, and speech. Each report holds
        the samples you approved for that kind of writing, then its rules. Your
        assistant handles the filing; you don’t manage a memo list. The names
        are an Office Space reference. The paperwork is less demanding.
      </p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>What do my connected assistants share?</summary>
      <p>
        Each can read your cover sheet and reports, samples included, exactly as
        you approved them. Keep private project context in its own tools. Milton
        doesn’t import another service’s memory or your conversation history.
      </p>
      <p>
        Samples are saved only when you say yes, and stored as written, names
        included. Rules are stored exactly as your assistant sends them; Milton
        never rewrites a rule or a sample.{" "}
        <a href="/privacy">Read the privacy policy.</a>
      </p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Will my assistant always write like me?</summary>
      <p>
        Not always. Milton keeps the samples and rules available. Ask your
        assistant to read them when you start work; the assistant still decides
        how closely to follow them.
      </p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Will I be charged after signing up?</summary>
      <p>
        No. Early access is currently free and we don’t collect payment details.
        The planned paid offer is $5.01 USD/month after a 30-day free trial. No
        credit card is required to try it, and you won’t be charged unless you
        subscribe.
      </p>
      <p>
        After an unsubscribed trial ends at paid launch, assistant reads and
        saves will pause. Your cover sheet and reports will remain available on
        the website to view and download.
      </p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Why the extra penny?</summary>
      <p>We’ve been assured the accounting software is working as intended.</p>
    </details>
    <details id="why-milton">
      <summary>Why does this exist?</summary>
      <p>
        Peter wanted his AI assistants to write like him. Somehow he ended up
        building them a filing department.
      </p>
      <p class="eyebrow">// An imaginary productivity review</p>
      <p>
        <strong>Reviewer:</strong> Walk us through a typical session.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Me:</strong> First I explain how I like to work. Then I remind
        it. Then it apologizes. Then I explain that I don’t need the apology.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Reviewer:</strong> How much actual work gets done?
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Me:</strong> About fifteen minutes.
      </p>
    </details>
  </section>
  <section class="closing">
    <p class="eyebrow">// Did you get that memo?</p>
    <h2>Let’s put that in a memo.</h2>
    <p>Your voice, ready for your next conversation. No all-hands required.</p>
    <a class="button" href="https://app.meetmilton.com/login">
      Try Milton free <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
    </a>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>

<style>
  :where(h1, h2:not(.sheet-heading), h3, p, figure) {
    margin: 0;
  }
  .hero {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1.15fr 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-16);
    align-items: center;
    padding-block: var(--space-20);
  }
  h1 {
    font-size: var(--text-hero);
    line-height: 1.18;
    letter-spacing: -0.05em;
    margin-top: var(--space-6);
    text-wrap: balance;
  }
  .intro {
    font-size: var(--text-lead);
    line-height: var(--leading-body);
    margin-top: var(--space-6);
    max-width: 36em;
  }
  .hero-aside {
    margin-top: var(--space-5);
    max-width: 40ch;
    font-size: var(--text-lead);
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .actions {
    margin-top: var(--space-6);
  }
  .access-note {
    margin-top: var(--space-3);
  }
  .memo-example {
    min-width: 0;
  }
  .example-name {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--space-2);
    padding: var(--space-3) var(--sheet-padding);
    border-bottom: 3px double var(--ink);
    font: var(--text-caption) / var(--leading-label) var(--font-mono);
  }
  .example-name span {
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .assistant-strip {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--space-3) var(--space-6);
    border-block: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    padding-block: var(--space-6);
    font-size: var(--text-small);
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .assistant-guides {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-2);
  }
  .guide-status {
    margin: 0;
  }
  .assistant-strip nav {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--space-2) var(--space-6);
  }
  .assistant-strip nav span {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-2);
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }
  .assistant-strip a {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    min-height: var(--touch-target);
    color: var(--ink);
    font-weight: 500;
  }
  .section {
    padding-block: var(--space-20);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hairline);
  }
  .section h2 {
    letter-spacing: -0.045em;
    font-size: var(--text-section);
    margin-block: var(--space-4) var(--space-6);
  }
  .section h2 span {
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .section-lead {
    max-width: 60ch;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-8);
    font-size: var(--text-lead);
  }
  .use-cases {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: var(--space-8);
  }
  .use-case {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    padding: var(--space-8);
    border-radius: var(--radius-card);
  }
  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .use-cases {
      row-gap: 0;
    }
    .use-case {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-rows: subgrid;
      grid-row: span 3;
    }
  }
  h3 {
    font-size: var(--text-title);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
  }
  .use-case p {
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .use-case .sample-rule {
    margin-top: var(--space-6);
    padding-top: var(--space-5);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    color: var(--ink);
    font-size: var(--text-body);
  }
  .steps {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: var(--space-8);
    padding: 0;
    margin: var(--space-8) 0;
    list-style: none;
    counter-reset: step;
  }
  .steps li {
    counter-increment: step;
  }
  .steps li::before {
    content: "0" counter(step);
    font: var(--text-caption) / var(--leading-label) var(--font-mono);
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .steps h3 {
    margin-top: var(--space-4);
  }
  .steps p {
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .conversation-steps,
  .pricing {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: var(--space-8);
  }
  .conversation blockquote {
    margin: var(--space-4) 0;
    font-size: var(--text-lead);
  }
  .steps p + p {
    margin-top: var(--space-3);
  }
  .pricing {
    align-items: start;
    gap: var(--space-16);
  }
  .price {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--space-3);
  }
  .price strong {
    font: var(--font-display-weight) var(--text-hero) / var(--leading-heading)
      var(--font-display);
  }
  .price span {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: var(--text-small);
  }
  .price-card ul {
    padding-left: var(--space-5);
    margin-block: var(--space-6);
  }
  .price-card li + li {
    margin-top: var(--space-2);
  }

  #how-it-works > .reading-note {
    max-width: none;
  }
  .reading-note {
    max-width: 75ch;
    margin-top: var(--space-8);
  }
  .control-section {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: var(--space-16);
  }
  .portability-copy {
    font-size: var(--text-lead);
  }
  .portability-aside {
    color: var(--muted);
    margin-block: var(--space-5);
  }
  .faq details {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    padding-block: var(--space-3);
  }
  .faq summary {
    cursor: pointer;
    list-style-position: outside;
    margin-inline-start: var(--space-5);
    min-height: var(--touch-target);
    padding-block: var(--space-3);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .faq details p {
    max-width: 75ch;
    margin-block: var(--space-2) var(--space-3);
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .closing {
    text-align: center;
    padding-block: var(--space-20);
  }
  .closing h2 {
    font-size: var(--text-section);
    margin-block: var(--space-4);
  }
  .closing p:not(.eyebrow) {
    color: var(--muted);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
  }
  @media (min-width: 861px) and (max-width: 1100px) {
    .hero {
      gap: var(--space-8);
      padding-block: var(--space-12);
    }
  }
  @media (max-width: 960px) {
    h1 {
      max-width: 660px;
    }
    .intro {
      max-width: 45ch;
    }

    .control-section {
      gap: var(--space-8);
    }
  }
  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .hero {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: var(--space-10);
      padding-block: var(--space-12);
    }
  }
  @media (max-width: 767px) {
    .control-section {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: var(--space-10);
    }
    .assistant-strip {
      display: grid;
      gap: var(--space-2);
    }
    .section,
    .closing {
      padding-block: var(--space-12);
    }
    .use-cases,
    .steps,
    .pricing,
    .conversation-steps {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: var(--space-6);
    }
    .hero {
      padding-block: var(--space-10);
      gap: var(--space-8);
    }
    .intro {
      font-size: var(--text-body);
      margin-top: var(--space-5);
    }
    .actions .button {
      padding-inline: var(--space-5);
    }
    .section-lead {
      font-size: var(--text-body);
    }
    .use-case {
      padding: var(--space-6);
    }
  }
  .memo-exchange {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
  }
  .memo-exchange dl {
    margin: var(--space-3) 0 0;
  }
  .memo-exchange dl > div {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 5.5rem minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: var(--space-3);
    padding-block: var(--space-3);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hairline);
  }
  .memo-exchange dl > div:last-child {
    border-bottom: 0;
    padding-bottom: 0;
  }
  .memo-exchange dt {
    font: var(--text-caption) / var(--leading-body) var(--font-mono);
    color: var(--muted);
    padding-top: 0.25rem;
  }
  .memo-exchange dd {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: var(--text-lead);
    line-height: var(--leading-body);
  }
  .memo-exchange dl > div:last-child dd {
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .memo-limit {
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
    color: var(--ink);
    font: var(--font-display-weight) var(--text-title) / var(--leading-heading)
      var(--font-display);
  }
  @media (max-width: 480px) {
    .memo-exchange dl > div {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: var(--space-2);
    }
    .memo-exchange dt {
      padding-top: 0;
    }
  }
  .employee-testimonial {
    margin: 0;
    align-self: center;
  }
  .employee-testimonial blockquote {
    max-width: 40ch;
    margin: var(--space-6) 0;
